// =============================================================================
// ARGUS — TARGET PHYSICAL SCHEMA (prisma/schema.target.prisma)
// =============================================================================
//
// THIS IS THE TARGET SCHEMA, NOT THE CURRENT/REAL SCHEMA.
//
// It models the 168-table / 19-domain-schema + geo target physical model
// (ARGUS_PHYSICAL_TABLE_CATALOG_v1.1_FROZEN.md, ARGUS_PHYSICAL_RELATIONAL_MODEL_v1.1_FROZEN.md,
// ARGUS_PHYSICAL_KEYS_CONSTRAINTS_INDEXES_v1.1_FROZEN.md, ARGUS_PHYSICAL_ACCESS_CONTROL_v1.1_FROZEN.md,
// ARGUS_PHYSICAL_ENUMS_REFERENCE_DATA_v1.1_FROZEN.md, ARGUS_MIGRATION_DECISION_REGISTER_v1.0_FROZEN.md).
//
// It is a DESIGN ARTIFACT for planning the migration away from the current
// `prisma/schema.prisma` (33-model, `public` schema, no RLS, no PostGIS). It is
// NOT wired into the application and MUST NOT be treated as the live schema.
//
// HARD RULES FOR ANYONE (HUMAN OR AGENT) TOUCHING THIS FILE:
//   1. NEVER run `prisma generate --schema prisma/schema.target.prisma` in a way that
//      overwrites the real generated client. The `generator target_client` block below
//      points at an isolated output path (`node_modules/.prisma/target-client-DO-NOT-USE`)
//      specifically so a stray `prisma generate` cannot collide with the production client
//      generated from `prisma/schema.prisma`.
//   2. NEVER run `prisma migrate dev` / `prisma migrate deploy` against production (or any
//      real database) using this file. There is no migration history for this schema — a
//      naive `migrate dev` would attempt to diff this against the live database and could
//      propose destructive changes. Real migration SQL for this target model lives (or will
//      live) under `prisma/target-migrations/<wave_folder>/migration.sql`, authored and
//      reviewed by hand, wave by wave — never generated blindly from this file.
//   3. `prisma/schema.prisma` and `prisma/migrations/` are the real, current, live-schema
//      artifacts. This file does not modify them, reference them as a Prisma `datasource`,
//      or share a migrations directory with them.
//   4. Everything Prisma 4.16.2 cannot represent natively (partial/filtered unique indexes,
//      CHECK constraints, exclusion constraints, table partitioning, triggers, functions,
//      views/materialized views, SECURITY DEFINER routines, append-only enforcement via
//      REVOKE, cryptographic integrity chaining, polymorphic FK validation) is preserved as
//      a `SQL_COMPLEMENTARY_REQUIRED` comment directly above the affected model/field,
//      pointing at the wave folder under `prisma/target-migrations/` where the real SQL
//      belongs. Nothing is silently dropped.
//
// Authority precedence for every column/type/FK/enum decision in this file:
//   ARGUS_PHYSICAL_TABLE_CATALOG_v1.1_FROZEN.md (+ v1.0 for tables inherited unchanged)
//   > ARGUS_PHYSICAL_RELATIONAL_MODEL_v1.1_FROZEN.md
//   > ARGUS_PHYSICAL_KEYS_CONSTRAINTS_INDEXES_v1.1_FROZEN.md
//   > ARGUS_PHYSICAL_ACCESS_CONTROL_v1.1_FROZEN.md (RLS — informational comments only, RLS
//     itself is not representable in Prisma and is NOT designed further in this file)
//   > ARGUS_PHYSICAL_ENUMS_REFERENCE_DATA_v1.1_FROZEN.md
//   > ARGUS_MIGRATION_DECISION_REGISTER_v1.0_FROZEN.md (D-01..D-08)
//
// Naming: models are PascalCase with `@@map("<physical_snake_case_table_name>")`; every
// field carries `@map("column_name")` to pin the exact physical column name even where it
// happens to already match Prisma's camelCase convention. `@@schema("<schema>")` pins the
// physical Postgres schema per the 19-schema + geo topology (Relational Model v1.1 Fase 1/11).
// `proj` (11 views/materialized views) is NOT modeled here — it is views-only, never a
// Prisma model schema (task instruction, consistent with "ningún rol de aplicación tiene
// privilegio de escritura sobre el schema proj" and Prisma 4.16.2 having no `view` block).
//
// PK strategy: UUIDv7 is the default (Relational Model v1.1 §1.2-1.4); Prisma 4.16.2 has no
// native `uuidv7()` — see the per-PK comment. `ice.emergency_profiles` and
// `security.audit_logs` are the sole UUIDv4 exceptions (P2-09 — avoids temporal-metadata
// leakage on the two most sensitive CRITICAL tables). Two tables use a composite PK instead
// of a surrogate `id` (`security.access_role_permissions`, `governance.automation_rule_incident_types`).
//
// =============================================================================

generator target_client {
  provider        = "prisma-client-js"
  previewFeatures = ["multiSchema"]
  output          = "../node_modules/.prisma/target-client-DO-NOT-USE"
}

datasource db {
  provider  = "postgresql"
  url       = env("DATABASE_URL")
  directUrl = env("DIRECT_URL")
  schemas   = ["identity", "institution", "capability", "ingest", "evidence", "incident", "risk", "command", "help", "mission", "resource", "comms", "alert", "ice", "community", "media", "security", "knowledge", "governance", "geo"]
}

// =============================================================================
// ENUMS
// =============================================================================
// 117 native enums total (116 per ARGUS_PHYSICAL_ENUMS_REFERENCE_DATA_v1.1_FROZEN.md §1
// reconciliation + `delivery_content_kind_enum`, already counted within that reconciliation
// but broken out explicitly here for clarity). `hazard_type_enum` and
// `administrative_area_kind_enum` are NOT modeled as enums — both were migrated to
// versioned reference tables (`governance.hazard_types`, `governance.administrative_area_kinds`)
// per P1-02/Corrección Obligatoria #8; see the Governance section below.
//
// Value-name provenance: where the frozen catalog gives an explicit value list inline
// (e.g. `-- PRIMARY | DERIVED`), that exact list is transcribed. Where the Enums Reference
// Data document gives only a value COUNT and a qualitative state description (e.g.
// "Vigente/revisado", 2 valores) without an explicit literal list, the value names below are
// inferred from that qualitative description and marked `// VALUES_INFERRED` — the member
// COUNT always matches the frozen count field; the literal spelling is a best-effort
// reconstruction, not a verbatim transcription, and should be reconciled against the real
// source enum definitions (if they exist elsewhere) before being used to generate SQL.
// =============================================================================

